$C9FB ; +1 ... +$14

$CA0F b InstrumentSlots 8 ; Eight instrument offsets per channel: 0, 10, ... 70
> MusicStartTune fills each channel's 8 bytes with 0, 10, ... 70 (the instruments 0-7, Instruments + offset); an order list byte $C0-$FD could change one (none does); PatternCommand reads them for $80-$87. Initial bytes: text of the source.

$CA27 c MusicStartTune ; Start tune A: silence, then the three channels from TuneTable
> SilenceAy; the order lists from TuneTable + 6 A into the channels' +1/+2; +9 = 1 (play once), +$0A = 0 (no transpose), +$0B = $FF (read the order list at the next frame), +$0C = 1, +$0D = $FF, +$0F = 0 (no ornament), +7/+8 = Instruments; InstrumentSlots = 0, 10, ... 70 three times; MusicPlaying = $FF.
