@module sequencer ; The tune sequencer: order lists, patterns, ornaments
@about One call of SequenceChannel a frame and channel: the note's frames count down; at 0 the pattern's next bytes are read (commands, then a note or a rest) and the note starts the voice. A pattern's $FF is met while the last note still sounds; the next frame takes the next order list entry, so patterns follow each other without a gap.

$CAF7 c SequenceChannel ; One frame of channel IY driving voice IX
> UpdateOrnament first. When the pattern has ended (+$0B): once more from its start while +9 counts down, else the next order list entry (ReadOrderLoop: $FE transpose, $FF the channel's end with +$0D = 0, $80-$BF the repeat, $C0-$FD an instrument slot, below $80 the pattern via PatternAddrLow / PatternAddrHigh). Then the note's frames +$0C go down; while the note lasts, a command byte at the pointer is done at once (PatternCommand); at 0, PatternCommand for each command, then the note: $7F a rest (only the frames), $7E a period word, else index + $0A + 12 into Periods (+$0E keeps it). The frames go to +$0C, the ornament state +$14 = ornament | $C0, and StartVoice runs with the instrument +7/+8, the period, the frames as sustain; not when the voice's flags have bit 7.
> 30 180 runs in the 9 builds; the order list 499, a new pattern 99, a note 2292, a rest 41 (l1q, 10 builds with sec-l1-s8). The slot command and the $7E period are not executed in any recording.
> Witness: L1 32775 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, sec-l1-s8, c1, load-l2-load-l5).
$CB00 PatternEnded ; once more, or the order list
$CB17 ReadOrderList ; +9 = 1
$CB21 ReadOrderLoop
$CB33 OrderNotTranspose
$CB3C OrderNotEnd
$CB49 OrderSetSlot ; $C0-$FD v: slot (bits 0-2) = v (not executed in any recording)
$CB56 OrderSlotStore
$CB5C OrderPattern ; a pattern number
$CB7C ContinuePattern
$CB82 CountNote
$CB94 ReadPatternLoop ; the note has ended: commands, then a note or a rest
$CBA5 PatternNote
$CBB6 PatternPitchedNote ; index = note + transpose + 12
$CBCA PatternNoteStart ; HL = the period
$CBF1 PatternRest ; $7F: only the frames

$CBFE c PatternCommand ; Do the pattern command at DE: instrument, ornament, end, or a skipped command
> $80-$87: the instrument +7/+8 = Instruments + InstrumentSlots[+0 + bits 0-2]; $88-$BF: the ornament +$0F = bits 0-3; $FF: +$0B = $FF (the pattern has ended; DE stays); $C0-$FE: skipped, $C2 one byte, the others four. DE moves past the command. 336 runs in the 9 builds; $88 and up 208, the ornaments 7 (l1q, 10 builds with sec-l1-s8); the skip is not executed in any recording.
> Witness: L1 360 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, sec-l1-s8, c1, load-l2-load-l5).
$CC1C PatternCommandHigh
$CC25 PatternCommandNotEnd
$CC30 PatternCommandSkip ; not executed in any recording

$CC38 c UpdateOrnament ; One frame of channel IY's ornament: the next semitone step into voice IX's period
> Nothing when the voice's flags have bit 7 or the state +$14 has bit 7 clear; number 0 clears bit 7. At the start (bit 6) and whenever the steps +$13 run out, OrnamentStart: the record at $C4A8 + 8 n (Ornaments), +$12 = its bits 3-5, +$13 = bits 0-2 + 1, the pointer at it, the period of the note itself; an ornament without bit 7 holds its last step instead of starting again. Each time the step's frames +$12 run out: the next step, +$12 = its bits 0-2, the period of +$0E + its bits 3-7 (SetPitch). 30 180 runs in the 9 builds; a step 2531, a start 1312 (l1q, 10 builds with sec-l1-s8).
> Witness: L1 32775 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, sec-l1-s8, c1, load-l2-load-l5).
$CC4C OrnamentRunning ; D = 7: the mask, and the high byte added at OrnamentStart
$CC6F OrnamentStep
$CC80 OrnamentStart ; HL = $BDA8 + $0700 (D) + 8 n = $C4A8 + 8 n
$CC9A OrnamentRestart
$CCB5 SetPitch ; voice IX's period = Periods[A] (the source's SETPITCH)
$CCBE SetPitchStore

@module effects
$CCC8 c MusicEffect ; Start effect A on a voice when no tune plays
> Nothing while MusicPlaying is not 0. IY = Effects + 13 A; PickEffectVoice gives IX (no carry: none, the effect is dropped); StartVoice with the period +$0A/+$0B and the sustain +$0C. Keeps all registers but AF. The lines from $CCF6 are in the leftover source text of ChannelA ("LD L,(IY+10) ... CALL SOUND ... POP IY / POP IX").
> Called from PlayEffect $7A97 through CallRam1: 385 runs in the 9 builds, 44 past the MusicPlaying test, 39 started.
> Witness: L1 429 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, sec-l1-s8, c1, load-l2-load-l5).
